

What is EBS?

Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS) is a persistent block storage service used with virtual machines (EC2 instances).

EBS is like a virtual hard disk attached to an EC2 server.

You attach EBS to an EC2 instance
Store OS, applications, databases, files
It behaves like a local hard drive in a computer


Real-Life Analogy

Think of:

EC2 Instance → Computer
EBS → Hard Disk (SSD/HDD)

Without EBS:

EC2 has no permanent storage

With EBS:

You can store files, OS, logs, databases safely.
⚙️ Key Features of EBS
1️⃣ Persistent Storage (Most Important)

Data remains safe even if:

EC2 stops
EC2 reboots

Unlike temporary storage.

👉 That’s why it's called persistent storage.

2️⃣ High Performance Storage

EBS provides:

Low latency
High-speed read/write
Suitable for databases

Common workloads:

MySQL
PostgreSQL
MongoDB
Enterprise applications
3️⃣ Snapshots (Backup System)

You can create:

👉 Snapshots = Backups

Snapshots:

Save current data state
Stored in Amazon S3
Can restore data anytime

Use cases:

Backup recovery
Disaster recovery
Clone volumes
4️⃣ Scalability (Elastic Nature)

You can:

Increase storage size
Increase IOPS
Change performance level

Without stopping the server.

This feature is called:

👉 Elastic Volumes

5️⃣ Data Safety (Replication)

EBS automatically:

Replicates data across servers
Inside one Availability Zone

So data is not lost if hardware fails.

📊 Types of EBS Volumes

There are 2 main categories:

🔹 SSD-Based Volumes (Fast)

Used for:

Databases
Boot volumes
Applications

Types:

Type	Use Case
gp3	General purpose (most common)
gp2	Older general purpose
io1 / io2	High-performance workloads
🔹 HDD-Based Volumes (Cheap Storage)

Used for:

Big data
Logs
Data warehouses

Types:

Type	Use Case
st1	Throughput optimized
sc1	Cold storage

These volume types allow cost vs performance optimization.

🧱 Components of EBS

There are 2 major components:

1️⃣ EBS Volume

Actual storage disk.

Example:

Volume size: 20 GB
Type: gp3
Attached to: EC2 instance

Used for:

OS installation
Database storage
File storage
2️⃣ EBS Snapshot

Backup of volume.

Example:

Snapshot: Backup of 20GB volume
Stored in: S3

Used for:

Backup
Restore
Clone server
🔄 How EBS Works (Step-by-Step)

Typical workflow:

Launch EC2 instance
Attach EBS volume
Install OS on volume
Store files & applications
Create snapshots for backup
⚖️ EBS vs Other AWS Storage

Very important for interviews.

Feature	EBS	S3	EFS
Type	Block	Object	File
Use	EC2 storage	File storage	Shared storage
Mount	One instance	Not mounted	Multiple instances
Persistence	Yes	Yes	Yes
